"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1739,"**
Narrated to us Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb: narrated to us my uncle (Ibn Wahb), who informed me from Makhramah, from his father, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa al-Ash'ari (RA), who said:
'Abdullah ibn 'Umar (RA) said to me, ""Did you hear your father narrating from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) regarding the time of acceptance of supplication on Friday?""
I said, ""Yes, I heard him say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say:
'It is between the time when the imam sits on the pulpit until the prayer is completed.'""

Narrated to us Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman: narrated to us my uncle, who informed me from Maymun ibn Yahya — and he is the son of the brother of Makhramah — from Makhramah, from his father, with this chain of narration similarly."
